WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.350
After the 1960s, Taiwan's economy grew rapidly.

00:00:03.597 --> 00:00:07.802
In the ports, cargo ships were loaded with exports.

00:00:07.802 --> 00:00:11.541
Dock workers busily moved box after box of goods.

00:00:11.731 --> 00:00:14.869
Factories opened one after another, and jobs increased.

00:00:15.109 --> 00:00:18.691
Many young people left the countryside to work in factories.

00:00:19.158 --> 00:00:22.722
At the end of the workday, crowds thronged the factory gates.

00:00:22.953 --> 00:00:25.447
The electronics industry slowly became an important industry.

00:00:25.539 --> 00:00:29.021
Tiny components were sold all over the world.

00:00:29.425 --> 00:00:32.215
People's lifestyles gradually changed.

00:00:32.215 --> 00:00:36.018
Streets grew livelier, and shops grew more numerous.

00:00:36.587 --> 00:00:39.893
Children put on new shoes and happily went to school.

00:00:40.385 --> 00:00:42.375
Later, the technology industry also grew rapidly.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:45.468
Products made in Taiwan reached the whole world.

00:00:45.992 --> 00:00:49.408
Engineers worked day and night in laboratories.

00:00:49.938 --> 00:00:53.022
This growth was called the Taiwan Economic Miracle.

00:00:53.572 --> 00:00:56.160
Amid change, society became more diverse.
